","The relationship between the standard enthalpy change of a reaction (ΔH) and the standard enthalpy changes of formation (ΔH₀) of the products and products is given by:

ΔH = Σ(n × ΔH₀(products)) - Σ(n × ΔH₀(reactants))

where 'n' is the stoichiometric coefficient of each species in the balanced equation.

In this case:

*  Reaction:  CaO(s) + H2O(l) → Ca(2O)(s)
