* **Coordation:** The core of the complex is the iron(III) ion (Fe³⁺) coordinated to the tetrapyrinate rings of the porphyrin. The four double rings of the porphyrine ring donate electrons to the iron ion.
* **Coordination Number:** The coordination number of Fe³⁺ in Fe(3)tph is typically **5**.  This means the iron ion is directly bonded to five donor groups.

