$$ \text{P}(X) = (x_1, p_1), (x_2, p_2), (x_3, p_3), (x_4, p_4), (x_5, p_5) $$
where $p_i > 0$ for all $i$ and $\sum p_i = 1$.
We have
$$ \text{E}(X^2) = \sum x_i^2 p_i = x_1^2 p_1 + x_2^2 p_2 + x_3^2 p_3 + x_4^2 p_4 + x_5^2 p_5 = 0 $$
