We are given that *n<sub>cl</sub> - n<sub>c</sub> ≈ 0.3*.  This is the difference between the cladding and core refractive indices.  We can use this to find the decay length.

**6.  Calculate the Decay Length**

The equation for the decay length is:

*L = 1 / (n<sub>cl</sub> * k)*

Since we know that *n<sub>cl</sub> - n<sub>c</sub> = 0.3*, we can express *n<sub>cl</sub>* as *n<sub>c</sub> + 0.3*.  Substituting this into the equation:

*L = 1 / ((n<sub>c</sub> + 0.3) * k)*

