The maximum change in wavelength occurs when θ = 0° (the photon is scattered head-to-face with the electron).  In this case, tan(0) = 0, so:

λ' = λ + (h/m₀c)

The change in wavelength is:

Δλ = λ' - λ = (h/m₀c)

The percentage change is:

% change = (Δλ / λ) * 100% = [(h/m₀c) / λ] * 100%

