*  T_g1 = initial temperature of the gases (1100°C)
*  T_g2 = final temperature of the gases (550°C)
*  T_w = temperature of the water (220°C) - constant during vaporization
*  c_g = specific heat of the gases (1.005 kg/kgK)
*  L = latent heat of vaporization of water (1858.5 J/kg)

**3. Calculate the Heat Lost by the Gases:**

The heat lost by the gases is equal to the change in their energy:

Q_loss = m_g * c_g * (T_g1 - T_g2)

